Confirmed. This commit shows the exact refactoring that merged the two separate `if/else` branches (each correctly wrapping `stripHtml(message) + link` or `escapeString(message) + link` inside `wrapInHtml()`) into a single ternary expression, but in doing so moved `+ link` outside the `wrapInHtml()` call — introducing the bug that the later commit fixes.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: d12f7fdbe42329c2e1e3faea654c884426255202

## Reasoning
(1) I used `git log --follow -p` on `LocalInspectionsPass.java` and grepped for the `wrapInHtml` tooltip-construction logic across its history, tracing the line from the original pre-bug form through to the fix. This is deterministic/structural evidence, not a style-based heuristic.

(2) The commit before the fix originally had two separate branches:
```java
if (message.startsWith("<html>")) {
  tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message) + link);
}
else {
  tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message) + link);
}
```
Both correctly placed `+ link` *inside* `wrapInHtml(...)`. Commit `d12f7fdbe4` collapsed these into a single ternary expression as part of a larger refactor (introducing `getFile()`, injected-language checks, etc.), but when consolidating the two branches it moved the closing parenthesis of `wrapInHtml(...)` to before `+ link`:
```java
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link ;
```
This left `link` concatenated outside the `<html>...</html>` wrapper — the exact bug that commit `8f5cb78051a` fixes by moving the closing paren back after `+ link`.

(3) The `git show` diff of `d12f7fdbe4` directly contains the before/after of this exact logic change at the same code location, and the "before" state in that diff is bug-free (matches semantics of the eventual fix), while the "after" state matches byte-for-byte the buggy line shown in the fix commit's diff. No intervening commits touched this line (confirmed via the `--follow -p` grep across all commits).

I'm confident in this identification — the line text in the fix's "before" state is an exact match to this commit's "after" state, with no other commits modifying that line in between.

